hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15740","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Abi Rashid, he said: I met the Tanukhi, the messenger of Heraclius to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), at Hims, and he was a neighbor of mine, a very old man who had reached senility or near it. I said: Will you not inform me about the message of Heraclius to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the message of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Heraclius? He said: Yes. The messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Tabuk, and he sent Dihyah al-Kalbi to Heraclius. When the letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him, he called the priests of Rome and its patricians, then closed a door upon himself and them, and said: This man has camped where you have seen, and he has sent to me calling me to three traits: calling me to follow him in his religion, or that we give him our wealth upon our land, and the land is our land, or we throw war to him. By Allah, you know in what you read of the scriptures that he will take what is under my feet. Come, let us follow him in his religion, or give him our wealth upon our land. They snorted with the snort of one man until they came out of their cloaks, and said: Do you call us to abandon Christianity or to be slaves to a Bedouin who came from the Hijaz? When he feared that if they left him they would corrupt Rome against him, he soothed them and barely did, and said: I only said that to you to know your firmness upon your affair. Then he called a man from the Arabs of Tujib who was over the Christian Arabs, and said: Call for me a man who preserves speech, Arabic in tongue, whom I will send to this man with the answer to his letter. He brought me, and Heraclius handed me a letter and said: Go with my letter to this man, and whatever of his speech you hear, preserve for me three traits from it: see whether he mentions his sheet which he wrote to me about anything, and see when he reads my letter whether he mentions the night, and see on his back whether there is anything that makes you suspicious. I set out with his letter until I came to Tabuk, and he was sitting among his companions resting on the water. I said: Where is your companion? It was said: Here he is. I walked forward until I sat before him, and handed him my letter, and he placed it in his lap. Then he said: From where are you? I said: I am one of Tanukh. He said: Do you incline to Islam, the Hanifiyyah, the religion of your father Ibrahim? I said: I am a messenger of a people, and upon the religion of a people, I will not turn from it until I return to them. He laughed and said: You do not guide whom you love, but Allah guides whom He wills, and He knows best those guided. O brother of Tanukh, I wrote a letter to Kisra and he tore it, and Allah will tear him and tear his kingdom. And I wrote to the Negus with a sheet and he destroyed it, and Allah will destroy him and destroy his kingdom. And I wrote to your companion with a sheet and he kept it, so the people will ever find might from him as long as good remains in life. I said: This is one of the three which my companion enjoined upon me, and I took an arrow from my quiver and wrote it on my sword sheath. Then he handed the sheet to a man on his left. I said: Who is your scribe who reads for you? They said: Mu'awiyah. And in the letter of my companion was: You call me to a garden whose width is the heavens and the earth, prepared for the righteous, so where is the Fire? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glory be to Allah, where is the night when the day comes? He said: I took an arrow from my quiver and wrote it on my sword sheath. When he finished reading my letter, he said: You have a right, and you are a messenger, and had we a reward with us we would have rewarded you with it; we are impoverished travelers. He said: A man from among the people called out, he said: I will reward him. He opened his baggage and brought a yellowish garment and placed it in my lap. I said: Who is the giver of the reward? It was said to me: Uthman. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will host this man? A youth from the Ansar said: I will. The Ansari stood and I stood with him, until when I left the assembly, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me and said: Come, O brother of Tanukh. I hurried toward him until I was standing in my place before him. He loosened his garment from his back and said: Here, proceed as you were commanded. I looked on his back, and there was a seal at the folds of the shoulder like a large cupping mark."
